Act as a Senior Automotive and IoT Cybersecurity Engineer conforming to the ISO/SAE 21434 standard. Perform a preliminary Threat Analysis and Risk Assessment (TARA), specifically Threat Identification and Damage Scenario formulation, for the system architecture modeled in Ansys Medini Analyze described below.

System Architecture Overview
The system is a multi-tier environmental/indoor monitoring platform featuring dual-path edge-to-cloud telemetry.

1. Central Processing Unit: Controller Indoor Unit (IUC).
2. Sensing Subsystem (connected to IUC): Particulate matter: PM_2.5, PM10; Toxic/ambient gases: CO, CO2, NO2, SO2, O3; Geolocation: Component GPS (bidirectional interface with IUC).
3. Actuation Subsystem: Actuator Status Display (controlled directly by IUC via Display In/Out lines).
4. Uplink Path A (Local Edge / Cellular): IUC <-->  Component Wi-Fi <-->  Controller Far edge device <-->  Component 4G <-->  Item/System Cloud server.
5. Uplink Path B (LPWAN): IUC <-->  Component LoRaWAN <-->  Component LoRa GW <-->  Item/System LoRa edge server <-->  Item/System Cloud server.
6. Backend and Consumer Tier: Item/System Cloud server <-->  Item/System User (dashboard / client application).


Task Scope and Objectives

1.	Apply the STRIDE threat modeling methodology systematically across: Physical/analog sensor interfaces and buses to the IUC; Local wireless channels (Wi-Fi, LoRaWAN, Cellular 4G, GPS RF signals); Intermediate computing nodes (Far edge device, LoRa Gateway, LoRa edge server); Cloud backend endpoints and end-user data delivery channels.
2.	Formulate clear Threat Scenarios and map each to a concrete Damage Scenario considering vehicle/system-level safety, operation, financial impact, and user privacy (SFOP).
Output Format
Provide the results in a structured Markdown table compatible with Ansys Medini Analyze TARA tables, using the following columns: Threat ID, Target Element / Interface, STRIDE Category, Compromised Asset and Property (Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability, Authenticity), Threat Scenario Description, Damage Scenario (Vehicle / Passenger / Operational Impact).
Ensure deep technical coverage of: Sensor data spoofing/tampering (especially safety-critical gases like CO and toxic pollutants) causing suppressed alerts or false status indications on the Status Display; Wireless jamming, replay, and eavesdropping attacks on LoRaWAN, 4G, Wi-Fi, and GPS; Compromise or lateral movement via intermediate processing nodes (Far edge device, LoRa Edge server); Man-in-the-Middle (MitM) and credential/session hijacking between Cloud server and User.
